<title>SLOVAKIA: Slovak central bank sets one-day repo tender.</title>
<headline>Slovak central bank sets one-day repo tender.</headline>
<dateline>BRATISLAVA 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Slovakia (NBS) said on Monday it had set a tender for a one-day securities repurchase for 10 a.m. (0900 GMT), offering banks liquidity at a fixed volume of 1.5 billion crowns.</p>
<p>The NBS said in a statement that the American-style tender would have a minimum rate of 9.7 percent.</p>
